              {
                "text": "ISSUE_KIND: streetlight\nISSUE: Damaged streetlight with missing/smashed globes on West 86th Street\nDETAILS: The photo shows a historic-style double-arm lamppost silhouetted against the bright sun in a blue sky, with the glass globes missing on both light fixtures. The user note adds that the pole number is 86-112 and both lamps have been smashed since last Friday, leaving the block dark at night.\nORGANIZATION: New York City Department of Transportation\nDEPARTMENT: Division of Street Lighting\nWHY: West 86th Street is a public municipal street within the City of New York. The New York City Department of Transportation (NYC DOT) is responsible for maintaining all municipal streetlights on city roadways.\nCOVERAGE_QUOTE: \"NYC DOT maintains nearly 400,000 streetlights throughout New York City, and is a national leader in using sustainable street lighting.\"\nCOVERAGE_URL: https://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/html/infrastructure/streetlights.shtml\nREPORTING_URL: https://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/html/contact/contact-form.shtml?transportation-issue=SL\nOFFICIAL_WEBSITE: https://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/html/home/home.shtml\nEMAIL: StreetLighting@dot.nyc.gov | https://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/downloads/pdf/sl11a.pdf\nPHONE: 311 | https://portal.311.nyc.gov/article/?kanumber=KA-02002\nPHOTO_LOOKS_DAYTIME: yes\nNOTE_SAYS_LIGHT_OUT: yes\nSOURCES:\nhttps://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/html/infrastructure/streetlights.shtml\nhttps://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/html/about/about.shtml\nhttps://portal.311.nyc.gov/article/?kanumber=KA-02002\nhttps://www.nyc.gov/html/dot/html/contact/contact-form.shtml?transportation-issue=SL",
